# An afternoon in the garden, cited by a corner and by no region at all.
#
# Nothing in this file says which garden, which bed or which side of anything
# these shots are on. Every one of them is placed by its coordinate and by where
# a boundary drawn somewhere else happens to run, which is why carving a new bed
# out of the garden changes what they belong to without changing a byte here.
#
# The shots are chosen so that each says something the others do not:
#
#   0002  well inside the ground a bed is later carved out of
#   0003  well inside the ground the garden keeps
#   0004  exactly on the line the carve is made along
#   0005  outside the garden altogether
#   0006  taken in the neighbouring plot's grid, landing in the garden
#   0007  a hundred millimetres outside the north boundary, on a float solution
#         good to two hundred and forty — nobody can say which side it is on
#   0008  retired, and so not evidence of anything
#   0009  taken in the neighbouring plot's grid, landing where the bed goes
#
# id at frame x y z method fix h-precision v-precision antenna session
